#!grafli v1
# Electronics 101 — concept overview
# Companion board to paper.md; how a wired board becomes light.

# ── entry / meta ──
@ box paper "Paper →︎\nthe full model" 60,60 220x80 %soft &link:./paper.md
@ box viewState "viewState persistence\nelements + wires + switch\nstates survive a reload\n(user's board wins)" 320,50 260x120 %plum &link:./paper.md#run-it
@ box lang "language EN / DE\nLabLang dict + LangSwitch\nwording and number format" 620,55 300x110 %forest &link:./paper.md#run-it
@ note legend 1010,60 """
left →︎ right: build →︎ solve →︎ show
colours mark pipeline stages
""" ~small

# ── pipeline (build → solve) ──
@ box parts "palette / parts\nbattery · switch · resistor\nLED · bulb · diode · transistor\nlogic gate · ammeter · voltmeter" 60,300 266x150 %teal &link:./paper.md#stated-simplifications
@ box nets "wires →︎ nets\nunion-find merges\nterminals into nodes\n2 per part, 3 for an NPN,\n5 for a gate package" 380,300 240x150 %primary &link:./paper.md#the-solver
@ box solver "DC nodal solver\nG v = i   (KCL)\nNorton stamps + Gaussian elim\ndiode / transistor / gate states\niterated to a fixed point" 700,285 290x170 %clay &link:./paper.md#the-solver
@ box perel "per-element V, I\npower = |V · I|\nper NPN: region, Ib, Ic\nper gate: func, Vcc, A B Y" 1070,300 240x150 %primary &link:./paper.md#measured-results

# ── outputs (show) ──
@ box probes "probes\niBattery · power · vTerm\npart<id> per watched part\nplot · recording · record" 700,530 270x130 %rose &link:./paper.md#run-it
@ box visuals "visuals\nLED glow ∝︎ current\nbulb glow ∝︎ power\nmeter pills read V / mA" 1070,520 270x140 %highlight &link:./paper.md#measured-results
@ box routing "wire routing (route.js)\nleads leave on the pad's side,\nthen only right angles\nscored: crossings > corners\n> buried runs > length\nGEOMETRY - never re-solved" 1440,300 290x170 %teal &link:./paper.md#wires-turn-corners
@ box plan "schematic, two sizes (M / Z)\nONE canvas: corner map, or\nthe whole window lettered\nrating (470 Ω) vs reading (5,1 mA)\nlabels dodge symbols, wires,\neach other (plan.js)" 1440,530 290x180 %rose &link:./paper.md#run-it

# ── scenarios ──
@ note scen 60,520 """
scenarios (keys 1-9)
1 led-basic - resistor tames an LED
2 series - two dim bulbs, 360 mA
3 parallel - two bright bulbs, 1282 mA
4 metering - ammeter in, voltmeter across
5 transistor - 0.8 mA commands 9.8 mA
6 diode-OR - a gate with no transistor
7 AND - two NPN in SERIES
8 OR - the same two in PARALLEL
9 XOR - OR and NAND, five transistors
  logic gate - the same XOR as ONE part
  half adder - two gates, SUM and CARRY
""" ~small &link:./paper.md#logic-gates

# ── the logic half ──
@ box gates "logic gates, from transistors\nswitch + 10k pull-down = an input\nseries = AND, parallel = OR\nXOR = (A or B) and not (A and B)" 380,520 280x150 %secondary &link:./paper.md#logic-gates
@ box package "the gate as a PACKAGE\n5 pins: VCC A B Y GND\nfunction is a property you set\noutput swings to the pads it HAS\n- unwire VCC and it stops" 720,880 300x160 %plum &link:./paper.md#the-gate-as-a-package
@ box adder "half adder\nXOR + AND on the same inputs\nSUM and CARRY = 1+1 = 10\nwhere this lab stops:\nno time, so nothing sequential" 1080,880 300x160 %clay &link:./paper.md#a-half-adder
@ box truth "truth table panel\none SOLVE per input row,\nrun on a copy of THIS board\nedit the circuit, edit the table" 60,880 290x150 %rose &link:./paper.md#logic-gates

# ── measurement path (hold → keep → cite) ──
@ box hand "instruments you hold\ntape 📏 · stopwatch ⏱ · voltmeter ⚡\nH walks the belt, a click is a pick\nthe palette rides here too" 60,700 300x150 %accent &link:./paper.md#instruments-you-hold
@ box pin "P keeps a reading\nnamed, then registered\nlike any other probe" 440,705 250x140 %accent &link:./paper.md#instruments-you-hold
@ box record "run record (.labrec)\nlab · scenario · seed · params\nprobe series + summaries\nand the command to redo it" 820,700 300x150 %secondary &link:./paper.md#the-same-contrast-run-as-a-study
@ box study "study: series-vs-parallel\n12 runs, 1.5 V - 12 V\nparallel: 3.18x the power,\n3.56x the current, 86% of the volts" 1220,700 320x150 %clay &link:./studies/series-vs-parallel/study.md
@ note mpath 1600,700 """
bottom row: measure -> keep -> cite
what a hand measures becomes a probe,
a probe becomes a record, a record is
what the paper is allowed to quote
""" ~small

# ── arrows ──
@ arrow parts -> nets
@ arrow nets -> solver "nodes"
@ arrow solver -> perel "v solved"
@ arrow perel -> visuals "drives"
@ arrow parts -> routing "pads + bodies" !dotted
@ arrow routing -> visuals "board AND schematic, one path"
@ arrow routing -> plan "the same paths, drawn flat" !dashed
@ arrow perel -> plan "ratings and readings" !dotted
@ arrow plan -> parts "click a symbol, select the part" !dashed
@ arrow perel -> probes "sampled"
@ arrow scen -> parts "build"
@ arrow scen -> gates "presets 5-9"
@ arrow gates -> parts "wiring only"
@ arrow perel -> truth "re-solved per row" !dashed
@ arrow truth -> gates "what it actually does"
@ arrow gates -> package "packaged"
@ arrow package -> adder "composed"
@ arrow package -> nets "5 terminals" !dotted
@ arrow truth -> adder "one column per output" !dashed
@ arrow viewState -> parts "restores board" !dashed
@ arrow lang -> visuals "labels + units" !dotted
@ arrow hand -> pin "kept"
@ arrow pin -> probes "registers"
@ arrow probes -> record "recorded"
@ arrow record -> study "read back"
